On 2008-09-02, Uggh <ron.a@vr-web.de> wrote:
> Is there a list of the equipment (armour, weapons, amulets, what
> else?) each monster (and therefore pet) is able to use? Or can anyone
> tell me how to look it up in the sources?

I don't know of any, but it's in m_dowear(), in worn.c, L359

Let's see what I can make of this:

The following can *not* wear anything:
  * Very Small monsters (< MZ_SMALL)
  * Handless monsters (M1_NOHANDS)
  * Animals (M1_ANIMAL)
  * Mindless monsters (except initial equipment) (M1_MINDLESS)

Anything remaining can put things on:

Rings:   never worn by monsters
Lenses:  never worn by monsters

Amulets: all remaining monsters
Helmets: all remaining monsters
Gloves:  all remaining monsters
Boots:   all remaining monsters except slithy (snake-like) monsters
         and centaurs

Things worn on the body have additional checks (cantweararm):

Shirts:  Only MZ_MEDIUM humanoids (excluding winged gargoyles and
         mariliths) which are not whirly and not incorporeal.
         [Shirts may not be put on if the monster is wearing a suit of
         armor]

Suits:   Only MZ_MEDIUM humanoids (excluding winged gargoyles and
         mariliths) which are not whirly and not incorporeal.
         Additionally, some monsters have a racial exception allowing
         them to wear certain suits (currently only hobbits able to
         wear any elven armor)

Cloaks:  Only MZ_SMALL monsters or MZ_MEDIUM humanoids (excluding
         winged gargoyles and mariliths) which are not whirly and not
         incorporeal. (Special exception covers all MZ_SMALL monsters
         which pass the first "can put things on" check.)

On equipment choices [m_dowear_type]:

Amulets: Only lifesaving or reflection (whichever they get first)
Helmets: Horned monsters can only wear helmets made of leather.
Boots:   Non-MFAST monsters will prefer speed boots to other boots.
         [Technically, they treat them as +20 better than they are.]

Generally, monsters will choose the armor they can wear with the best
AC.

It would be cool to convert this all into a list by monster type of
what equipment they'll use.

Weapons are handled separately, and I believe have been discussed
elsewhere.


